      "text": [
        "4915 - وَ قَالَ اَلنَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اَللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَ آلِهِ : \"لاَ يَحِلُّ لِأَحَدٍ أَنْ يُجْنِبَ فِي هَذَا اَلْمَسْجِدِ إِلاَّ أَنَا وَ عَلِيٌّ وَ فَاطِمَةُ وَ اَلْحَسَنُ وَ اَلْحُسَيْنُ وَ مَنْ كَانَ مِنْ أَهْلِي فَإِنَّهُ مِنِّي\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.4915 - The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) said:\n\"It is not permissible for anyone to be in a state of major ritual impurity (janabah) in this mosque except for Me (sw), Ali (as), Fatimah {s.a}, Hasan (as), Husayn (as), and whoever is from my family (as), for He (as) is part of Me (sw).\""
        ]
      }
    },
